WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.453 --> 00:00:16.003
"What are you talking about, Maggie?"

2
00:00:16.283 --> 00:00:16.983
Cole asked.

3
00:00:17.003 --> 00:00:18.505
"Why would Mr.

4
00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:20.086
Tate steal his own flavor?"

5
00:00:20.106 --> 00:00:23.569
"I see what Maggie's saying," Henry said.

6
00:00:23.589 --> 00:00:28.032
"What if bubble gum banana swirl isn't really Mr.

7
00:00:28.092 --> 00:00:29.033
Tate's invention?

8
00:00:29.974 --> 00:00:30.674
What if Mrs.

9
00:00:30.775 --> 00:00:32.296
Sweet came up with it first?"

10
00:00:33.592 --> 00:00:35.834
"Mr. Tate could be trying to frame Mrs.

11
00:00:35.894 --> 00:00:38.776
Sweet by saying she stole it from him," Maggie said.

12
00:00:38.796 --> 00:00:42.499
"He claims she doesn't want competition from the Dessert Den.

13
00:00:43.319 --> 00:00:46.081
But maybe he's the one who's trying to steal customers!"

14
00:00:47.062 --> 00:00:47.763
Cole shrugged.

15
00:00:47.783 --> 00:00:50.124
"I guess that's a pretty good motive.

16
00:00:50.885 --> 00:00:52.146
But we just talked to Mrs.

17
00:00:52.206 --> 00:00:57.009
Sweet. Wouldn't she have told us that bubble gum banana swirl is her flavor?"

18
00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:00.512
"She's really nice," Maggie reminded them.

19
00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:02.840
"Maybe she didn't want to get Mr.

20
00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:03.681
Tate in trouble.

21
00:01:04.501 --> 00:01:06.361
Even if he is a dirty flavor thief!"

22
00:01:07.462 --> 00:01:10.462
"I guess we should check out your idea, Maggie," Henry said.

23
00:01:10.482 --> 00:01:16.284
"Like I said, good detectives follow up on every lead and theory."

24
00:01:17.404 --> 00:01:18.765
Then he thought of another question.

25
00:01:18.785 --> 00:01:21.485
"But if Mrs.

26
00:01:21.605 --> 00:01:27.767
Sweet invented bubble gum banana swirl, why didn't she tell Patty how she came up with the flavor?"

27
00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:30.588
"Good question," Cole said.

28
00:01:31.492 --> 00:01:34.134
"Usually she has a story to go along with all her flavors.

29
00:01:34.514 --> 00:01:36.175
Like raspberry mint chip, for instance."

30
00:01:37.576 --> 00:01:38.597
Maggie grabbed her bike.

31
00:01:38.617 --> 00:01:43.320
"Just because Patty didn't know the story doesn't mean there isn't one," she said.

32
00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:46.122
"Let's go back to the Sweet Shop and ask Mrs.

33
00:01:46.162 --> 00:01:49.264
Sweet!" She raced off down the sidewalk.

34
00:01:50.125 --> 00:01:51.305
Henry and Cole followed.

35
00:01:53.207 --> 00:01:58.110
As they rounded the corner, Henry saw Robby and some other kids sitting on the grass, drinking sodas.

36
00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:00.892
"Wait!" he called to his friends.

37
00:02:02.144 --> 00:02:05.145
He wanted to stop and ask Robby why he was so mad at Mr.

38
00:02:05.165 --> 00:02:09.347
Tate. Plus, maybe one of the West Belltown kids had seen Mr.

39
00:02:09.367 --> 00:02:10.828
Tate do something suspicious.

40
00:02:11.968 --> 00:02:14.349
But Maggie and Cole were too far ahead to hear him.

41
00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:16.610
Henry shrugged and kept going.

42
00:02:17.691 --> 00:02:19.252
He waved at Robby as he passed him.

43
00:02:19.892 --> 00:02:21.513
But Robby just stared back at him.

44
00:02:25.734 --> 00:02:28.055
When they neared the Sweet Shop, Henry saw Mr.

45
00:02:28.095 --> 00:02:29.216
Moss standing outside.

46
00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:32.001
He was painting the shop's window frame.

47
00:02:32.021 --> 00:02:36.103
"Hello, kids," Mr.

48
00:02:36.143 --> 00:02:37.124
Moss said cheerfully.

49
00:02:37.144 --> 00:02:39.245
"Are you here to get some ice cream?"

50
00:02:39.265 --> 00:02:42.467
"Actually, we came to talk to Mrs.

51
00:02:42.507 --> 00:02:43.628
Sweet," Maggie said.

52
00:02:43.648 --> 00:02:45.809
"I haven't seen her yet.

53
00:02:46.569 --> 00:02:49.091
I just got here a few minutes ago myself," Mr.

54
00:02:49.131 --> 00:02:49.651
Moss said.

55
00:02:49.671 --> 00:02:53.953
"I wanted to surprise her by getting started on this painting she asked me to do."

56
00:02:54.954 --> 00:02:56.655
He held up his paintbrush and smiled.

57
00:02:56.675 --> 00:02:58.396
"She might be inside."

58
00:02:59.776 --> 00:03:03.338
The kids left their bikes leaning against the lamppost and entered the Sweet Shop.

59
00:03:05.499 --> 00:03:06.880
Patty was still behind the counter.

60
00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.641
"Hi. Is Mrs.

61
00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:10.362
Sweet around?"

62
00:03:10.642 --> 00:03:11.402
Henry asked her.

63
00:03:11.422 --> 00:03:13.503
"Sorry, no.

64
00:03:13.644 --> 00:03:15.725
She left half an hour ago to run an errand."

65
00:03:16.845 --> 00:03:18.066
Henry was disappointed.

66
00:03:18.866 --> 00:03:20.407
They really needed to talk to Mrs.

67
00:03:20.447 --> 00:03:24.770
Sweet! "We were wondering about something," he said to Patty.

68
00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:29.072
"How long has bubble gum banana swirl been on the menu?"

69
00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:31.381
"Hmm, let me think."

70
00:03:32.381 --> 00:03:33.441
Patty tapped her chin.

71
00:03:33.461 --> 00:03:36.443
"I remember serving it on Monday afternoon.

72
00:03:37.443 --> 00:03:39.164
Mrs. Sweet must have added it that morning."

73
00:03:39.184 --> 00:03:43.205
"Monday?" Henry traded a look with his friends.

74
00:03:43.225 --> 00:03:45.886
"Do you kids want to order anything?"

75
00:03:46.167 --> 00:03:47.287
Patty glanced outside.

76
00:03:47.307 --> 00:03:49.868
"If so, you should probably do it now.

77
00:03:50.568 --> 00:03:52.849
It looks like a whole crowd of customers just arrived."

78
00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:55.430
Henry looked out the front window.

79
00:03:56.511 --> 00:03:58.432
A van had just stopped by the curb outside.

80
00:03:59.708 --> 00:04:01.949
A bunch of little kids were jumping out of it.

81
00:04:01.969 --> 00:04:04.931
"No, thanks," he told Patty.

82
00:04:06.132 --> 00:04:08.713
The little kids rushed in, along with a couple of adults.

83
00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:13.936
As they clustered around the counter, Henry and his friends moved over to a private corner.

84
00:04:13.956 --> 00:04:17.678
"Now we know how long Mrs.

85
00:04:17.758 --> 00:04:19.699
Sweet has had that flavor," Cole said.

86
00:04:19.719 --> 00:04:22.281
"But we don't know when Mr.

87
00:04:22.401 --> 00:04:24.302
Tate invented it," Henry said.

88
00:04:24.322 --> 00:04:28.084
"We need to find out when he painted his sign.

89
00:04:28.848 --> 00:04:32.409
If it was after Monday morning, he's probably guilty.

90
00:04:33.349 --> 00:04:36.410
But if it was before Monday, then he's innocent."

91
00:04:37.491 --> 00:04:38.371
"He's guilty."

92
00:04:38.691 --> 00:04:39.791
Maggie sounded confident.

93
00:04:39.811 --> 00:04:41.332
"Let's go ask him."

94
00:04:41.352 --> 00:04:43.973
"Do you think he'll tell us the truth?"

95
00:04:44.233 --> 00:04:45.993
Cole wondered as they headed toward the door.

96
00:04:47.194 --> 00:04:49.915
They had to stop a few times to dodge excited little kids.

97
00:04:51.215 --> 00:04:51.975
Maggie shrugged.

98
00:04:51.995 --> 00:04:54.316
"Why wouldn't he tell us the truth?

99
00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:58.597
He thinks we're on his side, remember?"

100
00:05:00.017 --> 00:05:01.997
Outside the Sweet Shop, nobody was around.

101
00:05:02.798 --> 00:05:03.278
Even Mr.

102
00:05:03.318 --> 00:05:04.258
Moss had disappeared.

103
00:05:05.458 --> 00:05:06.999
Cole looked around in confusion.

104
00:05:07.019 --> 00:05:09.439
"Hey," he said.

105
00:05:09.459 --> 00:05:11.480
"Where are our bikes?"

106
00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:13.380
Just then Mr.

107
00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:17.302
Moss hurried into view from the alley between the Sweet Shop and the building next door.

108
00:05:18.282 --> 00:05:19.762
He was holding a new can of paint.

109
00:05:19.782 --> 00:05:22.683
"Hello again, kids," he said.

110
00:05:22.703 --> 00:05:24.263
"Did you find Mrs.

111
00:05:24.303 --> 00:05:27.125
Sweet?" "No," said Maggie.

112
00:05:27.145 --> 00:05:29.388
"And now someone stole our bikes!"

113
00:05:30.469 --> 00:05:31.671
"Wait!" Cole called.

114
00:05:31.691 --> 00:05:32.953
"I see them!

115
00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:34.414
Look—over there!"

116
00:05:35.436 --> 00:05:37.639
Henry looked where Cole was pointing and gasped.

117
00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:41.443
Their bikes were lying in a jumbled pile behind the van!
